Subject: [PATCH] fix(quality): resolve Pylint findings

Pylint 8.25/10 (after the security fix) -> 10.00/10, without disabling
any check:
- W0102: logs=[] default replaced by logs=None (no list shared by calls).
- W0603: results and the active formula (settings dict) are updated in
  place instead of being rebound with global statements.
- R1732/W1514: files are opened with "with" and encoding="utf-8".
- W0622: the credits parameter/variable no longer shadows the builtin.
- W0611, C0103, C0121, C0209, C0114/C0116: unused sys import removed,
  printShortlist renamed to print_shortlist, truthiness test instead of
  == True, f-string, module and function docstrings.

Defects found by running the program and writing the tests:
- Applicant data is validated (GPA 0-10; credits and income finite and
  not negative). U003 (GPA 12.5, negative credits and income) is now
  reported and skipped instead of being shortlisted with score 119.0.
- The formula prompt comes before scoring, so one formula is applied to
  every applicant, and an error for one applicant no longer stops the run.
- load_results() keeps the current results if the file does not hold
  valid results.
- main() only runs under if __name__ == "__main__", so importing the
  module has no side effects.

Results-file write errors (found in code review, not by a tool):
- persist_results() catches OSError, logs "Could not save results to
  <file>: <error>" and returns False, or True once the file is written.
  The in-memory results are left untouched.
- main() reads the file back only after a successful save, so an older
  file cannot replace this run's results; otherwise the shortlist is
  printed from memory.

Tests extended to 46: formula security, scoring, eligibility and
validation, persistence including write failures, the shortlist, and
main() and import behaviour. The Pylint report is added and the Bandit
report regenerated (no issues). Flake8 still reports E302 x13 and E305 x1;
they are fixed in the next commit.
